1
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:29,946
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

2
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:32,157
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

3
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:36,119
(DOOR RATTLES, CREAKS OPEN)

4
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,627
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

5
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:49,340
-(GRUNTS)
-♪ (MUSIC STOPS) ♪

6
00:00:51,634 --> 00:00:52,635
What the fuck?

7
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:55,055
It's time to get up, Junior.

8
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:57,140
JOHN STEWART JUNIOR:
What did the Guardians say?

9
00:00:58,391 --> 00:01:00,185
About what?

10
00:01:00,226 --> 00:01:03,229
We got four dead aliens
on a football field.

11
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:05,273
Another one just blew up
half the sheriff's station.

12
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:07,150
Oh yeah,
I'm not calling the Guardians.

13
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:09,027
JOHN: Then what the fuck
are you doing here, Hal?

14
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,029
-I'm training you.
-(BUCKET CLANGS)

15
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:12,447
(DOOR CLOSES)

16
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:15,784
(DOOR RATTLES)

17
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:19,954
No, no, really.
You just take your time.

18
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:21,331
What the fuck
are we doing, Jordan?

19
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:22,999
What're you talking about?
You've been busting my balls

20
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:24,501
for a month to learn how to fly.

21
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:26,294
-Today's the day
you're gonna learn.
-We got a case to work.

22
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:28,421
Jesus Christ Almighty.

23
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:30,131
Unclench.

24
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:32,801
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

25
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:38,598
You ready?

26
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:53,113
(DISTANT TRAIN HORN BLARING)

27
00:01:56,449 --> 00:01:57,659
You fly.

28
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:58,701
Fly?

29
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:01,579
-Fly.
-(CHUCKLES)

30
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:04,207
(SCOFFS) That's it?
Just... just fly?

31
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:06,626
Oh, no, no, no, no.
I-- I-- I'm sorry.

32
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:07,710
-Fly, please.
-Ah.

33
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:09,671
HAL JORDAN: Look,
it's supposed to be instinctual.

34
00:02:09,712 --> 00:02:11,297
Just concentrate.

35
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:13,174
-Me, I'm a fighter pilot.
-JOHN: So I've heard.

36
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:14,968
When I think "fly,"
it's automatic.

37
00:02:15,009 --> 00:02:16,511
See-- Just concentrate.

38
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:19,222
-Think flight.
-JOHN: Mm-hmm.

39
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:20,723
Great. Thank you.

40
00:02:27,897 --> 00:02:29,399
Back up a little bit.

41
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,319
♪ (LOW BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

42
00:02:39,659 --> 00:02:43,872
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

43
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:48,751
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

44
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:57,051
(INHALES DEEPLY)

45
00:02:57,093 --> 00:02:58,303
(GRUNTS)

46
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:02,390
(RING WARBLING SOFTLY)

47
00:03:03,266 --> 00:03:04,684
(BIRD CHIRPING)

48
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,477
(WINGS FLAPPING)

49
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:08,771
What the fuck is that?

50
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:12,859
Uh, I think that's a bird, sir.

51
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:14,444
Uh...

52
00:03:14,485 --> 00:03:16,404
Why don't you drop
the "sir" bullshit.

53
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:18,781
-We both know you don't mean it.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

54
00:03:18,781 --> 00:03:19,824
Whatever you say.

55
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:21,326
(CHIRPING)

56
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:23,703
♪ (MUSIC FADING) ♪

57
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:26,789
-(RING PULSING)
-AUTOMATED VOICE:
Ring nearing depletion.

58
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:30,293
-All right, new lesson.
Gratis. Gimme the ring.
-(RING HUMS WEAKLY)

59
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:32,962
-Come on.
-(CHIRPING)

60
00:03:34,172 --> 00:03:35,924
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

61
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:38,885
♪ (POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

62
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:40,303
Is there a problem?

63
00:03:41,804 --> 00:03:44,641
-No. No.
-♪ (BROODING STRING
MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

64
00:03:46,142 --> 00:03:47,936
Ring gets low on charge,
there's a...

65
00:03:47,977 --> 00:03:49,687
(BIRD CHIRPING)

66
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,314
...one-time trick re-up.

67
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:54,317
You just gotta...

68
00:03:54,817 --> 00:03:56,611
(CHIRPING)

69
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,489
Just gotta hit it flush.

70
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:02,575
-(RING HUMS SHARPLY)
-AUTOMATED VOICE:
Ring charge, five percent.

71
00:04:02,617 --> 00:04:04,953
-All right.
-♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

72
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:06,287
New flight plan.

73
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:09,832
-I booked you a window.
-I don't understand.

74
00:04:09,874 --> 00:04:11,125
HAL: On an airplane.

75
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:13,044
There's seats near the windows,
there's seats near the aisles,

76
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:14,337
and there's seats
in the middle too.

77
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:16,047
Nobody wants those, uh--

78
00:04:16,089 --> 00:04:19,634
Look, the point is I need
the lantern to charge the ring.

79
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:22,428
I need you
to go back to Coast City
to my place and get it.

80
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:24,973
The, uh, address is on the back
and the...

81
00:04:25,014 --> 00:04:26,599
the key is out front
under the rock.

82
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:28,351
But, Hal,
this is already booked.

83
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:30,436
-(BIRD CHIRPING)
-(WINGS FLAPPING)

84
00:04:30,478 --> 00:04:32,188
Wait, so what would you
have done if I could fly?

85
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:34,565
Well, you didn't fly, did you?
So, it doesn't really matter.

86
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,734
Now get yourself ready.
I need that lantern.

87
00:04:38,027 --> 00:04:39,279
Oh, uh...

88
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:42,532
One more thing.
Uh, feed Earl for me, would you?

89
00:04:42,573 --> 00:04:45,410
-His food's in the icebox.
-And what's Earl?

90
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:46,869
-Is it a dog? Cat?
-(CHIRPING)

91
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:49,664
HAL: You know what?
And one more training exercise.

92
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:53,251
Take that... that bird with you
and bring it back alive.

93
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:55,211
You lose concentration,
it disappears.

94
00:04:55,211 --> 00:04:56,754
It disappears, you fail.

95
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:58,881
Don't fail.

96
00:05:00,216 --> 00:05:01,426
(CHIRPING)

97
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:02,802
And what are you gonna be doing?

98
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:05,638
HAL: Enjoying
not answering your questions.

99
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:07,598
(DOOR CLOSES)

100
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:13,813
♪ (BROODING GUITAR
RIFF PLAYING) ♪

101
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:24,741
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

102
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:29,996
♪ (PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

103
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:49,432
♪ (BROODING MUSIC OVERLAPPING) ♪

104
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:08,868
(SPRINKLERS HISSING)

105
00:06:11,287 --> 00:06:14,457
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

106
00:06:31,015 --> 00:06:32,392
(CROWBAR THUDS)

107
00:06:32,975 --> 00:06:34,018
(GRILLE CLATTERS)

108
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:50,368
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

109
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:53,788
AUTOMATED VOICE:
You've reached the Rushville
Sheriff's Department.

110
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:57,834
If this is an emergency,
please hang up and dial 911.

111
00:06:57,875 --> 00:06:59,669
Otherwise,
please leave a message

112
00:06:59,710 --> 00:07:01,504
and someone
from the department...

113
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:03,673
♪ (INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

114
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:09,762
(KEYS JINGLING)

115
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:23,693
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

116
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:28,531
(RING WARBLES)

117
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:35,413
♪ (LOW BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

118
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:37,832
HAL: There you are.

119
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,709
-(RING PULSING)
-AUTOMATED VOICE: This ring
will soon run out of charge.

120
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:41,043
-Fuck.
-AUTOMATED VOICE: Three,

121
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:42,879
two, one.

122
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,341
-(EXHALES SHARPLY)
-(CAR DOOR CLOSES)

123
00:07:47,383 --> 00:07:50,052
-(CAR ENGINE REVVING)
-(TIRES SCREECHING)

124
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:54,974
♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

125
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:59,061
(TIRES SCREECHING)

126
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:14,076
(KERRY KANE SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY ON MICROPHONE)

127
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:18,414
-(CITIZEN SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)
-(OVERLAPPING CHATTER)

128
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:20,541
(CHATTER STOPS)

129
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:22,210
-(DOOR HINGES CREAKING)
-♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

130
00:08:24,128 --> 00:08:26,589
Were you talking about me?

131
00:08:26,589 --> 00:08:29,717
-(CHAIRS CREAKING)
-(FAINT MURMURS)

132
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:31,219
You were talking about me.

133
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:41,771
(SOFTLY) Excuse me.

134
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:44,607
Excuse me.

135
00:08:45,858 --> 00:08:46,901
Excuse me.

136
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:50,238
(CLEARS THROAT)

137
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:54,158
(FAINT MURMURS CONTINUE)

138
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:55,868
Carry on.

139
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:02,375
We were just talking
about whether to go ahead

140
00:09:02,416 --> 00:09:04,252
with this Friday's
football game.

141
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:06,712
Would that be traumatizing,

142
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:09,799
or could it help
pull the community together?

143
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:12,927
Coach,
you were about to say something.

144
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:18,015
Right. Yeah. Um...

145
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:20,476
I've been talking to the boys,

146
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:24,146
and, uh,
they're pretty shook up.

147
00:09:24,188 --> 00:09:26,524
-This is also something
they've been working for...
-(QUIETLY) Hey.

148
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:28,442
-since two-a-days.
-(WHISPERS INDISTINCTLY)

149
00:09:28,484 --> 00:09:30,069
COACH: Uh, I mean... (SIGHS)

150
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:32,154
-I guess I wonder what we're...
-BILL MACON: (WHISPERS)
Sorry. Sorry.

151
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:36,200
...what we're teaching 'em
if we just pack it up
and forfeit.

152
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:39,453
-KERRY: Yeah, I think that's
what we're trying to figure out.
-(QUIETLY) Good news.

153
00:09:39,495 --> 00:09:42,081
-I got the judge
to drop your assault charges.
-(COACH RESUMES SPEAKING)

154
00:09:42,123 --> 00:09:43,874
-Well, I appreciate that.
-(CHUCKLES)

155
00:09:43,916 --> 00:09:46,877
-How much is it gonna cost me?
-Oh, no. It's on the house.

156
00:09:46,919 --> 00:09:49,839
KERRY:
And, obviously, we're worried...

157
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:52,633
Good news is you're free
to go back to Coast City.

158
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:55,303
Or anywhere else you feel like
going for that matter.

159
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:57,555
What was everyone talking about
when I came in here?

160
00:09:57,597 --> 00:10:01,309
KERRY: ...well-placed,
to go ahead with the game
and playing.

161
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:02,685
Five people just died here.

162
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:05,521
An alien blew himself up
at the sheriff's station.

163
00:10:05,563 --> 00:10:07,106
That's a lot to process.

164
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:07,982
Did your wife tell you

165
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:10,109
that alien was chirping
about vengeance

166
00:10:10,151 --> 00:10:12,069
before he blew himself up?

167
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:17,742
Here's what I'd really like
to talk to you about.

168
00:10:17,783 --> 00:10:19,702
I ended up
on that football field

169
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,329
because of a hunch. Hmm.

170
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:22,455
Just a gut feeling

171
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:24,915
that it was
gonna be extraterrestrial.

172
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:28,210
But your father's men,
they shot four people.

173
00:10:28,252 --> 00:10:31,672
And yet, those guys' friend
ends up being an alien?

174
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:33,883
(COACH SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

175
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:35,635
Is that a... a question or...

176
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:37,219
Uh, it's just a roundabout way
of saying

177
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:40,014
you don't shoot people
because of a gut feeling.

178
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:44,393
-I... I wouldn't know--
-HAL: No, I'm telling you.

179
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:46,228
-You don't.
-Okay.

180
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:49,649
So, how is it that father's men
knew who to target?

181
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:50,941
You'd have to ask him,
I don't--

182
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:52,109
HAL: I'm asking you
as my attorney,

183
00:10:52,151 --> 00:10:53,736
someone who cares
about my wellbeing,

184
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:55,404
and apparently,
my travel schedule.

185
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:56,530
We are still talking

186
00:10:56,572 --> 00:10:58,491
with attorney-client privilege,
I presume.

187
00:10:58,532 --> 00:11:00,242
KERRY: Excuse me, honey?

188
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:01,410
BOTH: Yes?

189
00:11:02,828 --> 00:11:04,580
KERRY: I was talking
to my husband.

190
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:05,956
Oh. Oh, yeah. Of course.

191
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:08,417
If you two
are gonna keep talking,

192
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:10,336
I'm gonna need
Mr. Jordan to leave.

193
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:12,254
-He started it.
-Well...

194
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:15,007
I've got about 30 seconds
of patience left.

195
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:16,550
I only need 40.

196
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:18,636
KERRY: And I'll be happy
to give them to you

197
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:20,096
when we're done here.

198
00:11:21,138 --> 00:11:23,057
Well, how long
is that gonna take?

199
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:27,103
-(MICROPHONE SCREECHING)
-It'll take as long as it takes.

200
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:29,605
Yeah, I don't think
I can keep quiet that long.

201
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:31,941
-(CELL PHONE RINGING)
-(FAINT CHATTER)

202
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:35,861
Oh, uh, sorry,
I gotta... I gotta take this.

203
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:38,239
Yeah. As you were.

204
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:40,783
Talk to me, Junior.

205
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,868
-JOHN: This house is insane.
-(BIRD CHIRPING)

206
00:11:42,910 --> 00:11:44,453
HAL: That's what you called
to tell me?

207
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:46,664
JOHN: No, no,
I can't find the key.

208
00:11:46,706 --> 00:11:48,958
HAL: Well, did you look
under the rock?

209
00:11:50,584 --> 00:11:52,086
Which rock, Hal?

210
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:54,213
HAL: To the left
of the door under the bush.

211
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:55,506
(GRUNTS)

212
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,133
-It looks like a potato
with a smile.
-(CAR ENGINE STARTING)

213
00:11:57,174 --> 00:11:59,760
HAL: Or a frown
if I left it upside down.

214
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,137
Potato rock.

215
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:04,098
♪ (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

216
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:12,148
(KEY CLATTERS)

217
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:16,569
(CHIRPS)

218
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:17,987
So, how's it going over there?

219
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:21,407
I get the feeling
everyone wants me gone.

220
00:12:23,033 --> 00:12:27,371
Kinda makes me feel
like I need to stick around.

221
00:12:27,413 --> 00:12:28,873
It would make you think that.

222
00:12:28,914 --> 00:12:30,458
HAL: The lantern's in my closet.

223
00:12:30,499 --> 00:12:33,294
If you're at the front door,
it's upstairs to the left.

224
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:39,175
So, how much
do Lanterns get paid anyway?

225
00:12:39,175 --> 00:12:40,217
Not enough.

226
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:42,386
I can tell you that.

227
00:12:42,428 --> 00:12:46,015
-JOHN: Well,
your house begs to differ.
-(DOOR RATTLING)

228
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:47,933
(GLASS CLATTERING)

229
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:49,935
-JOHN: What the hell was that?
-Don't worry about it.

230
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:54,148
I got the house from a rich guy.
Saved his kid.

231
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:56,400
His dad felt like shit
because he couldn't help.

232
00:12:56,442 --> 00:13:00,196
I didn't want to emasculate him
anymore, so I...

233
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:06,410
let him buy me a house.

234
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:09,205
So, when are you actually going
to move into this place?

235
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,290
What are you talking about?

236
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:13,542
I've lived in that house
for eight years.

237
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:16,754
-JOHN: You've got no furniture.
-(GRUNTS) I have a bed.

238
00:13:16,796 --> 00:13:18,130
I found your room.

239
00:13:18,172 --> 00:13:20,299
HAL: The lantern's in a box
in the back of the closet.

240
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:22,259
Go into the hallway
and turn right.

241
00:13:23,552 --> 00:13:25,471
(PANTING)

242
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:33,979
