283
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:53,369
Got your favorite.
Uh, beef and bison.

284
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:04,421
Earl?

285
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:12,054
(CHIRPING)

286
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:14,974
Hey, Earl, listen, I, uh...
I don't know where you are,

287
00:16:15,015 --> 00:16:19,228
but, um, kinda ready
to be done with this meat.

288
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:20,896
♪ (MUSIC RISES) ♪

289
00:16:20,896 --> 00:16:24,233
-(EARL GROWLS)
-(SOFTLY) Jeez!

290
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:25,859
-(BIRD SCREECHING)
-♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

291
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:29,780
(HISSES, GROWLS)

292
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:31,657
What the hell is wrong
with you, Jordan?

293
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:34,868
(EARL GROWLING)

294
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:37,246
What's up, man?
Hey, Earl. I'm, uh...

295
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:41,291
I'm John, and I'm...
I'm here to feed you.

296
00:16:41,333 --> 00:16:43,961
-Just don't eat my bird.
-(EARL GROWLS)

297
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:45,295
All right.

298
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:48,007
-There you...
-(CHOMPS)

299
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:50,467
JOHN: You know,
uh, once upon a time,

300
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:52,678
hamburgers used
to be my thing, too.

301
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,681
-(ROARS)
-Whoa! Hey!

302
00:16:55,723 --> 00:16:57,182
(BELLOWS, MUNCHES)

303
00:16:58,475 --> 00:16:59,560
