337
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:27,416
-(CAR HORNS HONKING)
-(TIRES SCREECHING)

338
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,794
♪ (INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

339
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,422
(CAR HORN BLARING)

340
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:38,510
(CAR HORNS BLARING)

341
00:19:40,637 --> 00:19:42,347
(TIRES SCREECHING)

342
00:19:47,686 --> 00:19:50,689
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

343
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:51,815
(CHIRPING)

344
00:19:58,947 --> 00:19:59,948
(DRIVER YELPS)

345
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:07,706
(TIRES SCREECHING)

346
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:10,292
-(ECHOING THUD)
-♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

347
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:16,840
(POLICE SIREN WAILING)

348
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:23,305
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

349
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:26,350
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

350
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:36,485
(CAR ENGINE RUNNING)

351
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:51,291
Is this about me
not being on the insurance?

352
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:53,502
(SNIFFS)

353
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:55,170
It is pretty much
exactly what it looks like.

354
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,463
But in my defense,

355
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:58,382
I wanted to talk to you
about this at the meeting,

356
00:20:58,423 --> 00:20:59,675
and you shushed me.

357
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:03,845
You're killing me, Jordan.
You know that?

358
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:06,682
Just a slow, painful death.

359
00:21:06,682 --> 00:21:09,351
There's more going on here
than you realize.

360
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:11,687
You mean like you going
to the stadium

361
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:14,523
and dragging these corpses
through the metal detector,

362
00:21:14,564 --> 00:21:18,402
which you now realize
is actually an alien detector?

363
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:20,654
Uh, let me rephrase.

364
00:21:20,696 --> 00:21:24,157
You obviously realize
exactly what's going on here.

365
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:27,202
Congratulations.
You've caught up to me.

366
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:29,788
Now, would you just please
let me do my job?

367
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:32,291
Is this a good time
to talk about jurisdiction?

368
00:21:32,332 --> 00:21:33,417
Because you seemed
really hung up

369
00:21:33,458 --> 00:21:34,751
on what was terrestrial
and what wasn't.

370
00:21:34,793 --> 00:21:37,212
-And as far as--
-Where are you going
with these guys?

371
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:38,714
To visit your father-in-law.

372
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:45,512
May I just say,
that is a profoundly bad idea.

373
00:21:45,554 --> 00:21:48,140
Did he put up those detectors?

374
00:21:48,181 --> 00:21:50,058
-He did.
-Do you know where he got them?

375
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:51,727
-I do not.
-You're not even curious?

376
00:21:51,768 --> 00:21:54,813
It's not against the law
to be obsessed with aliens.

377
00:21:54,855 --> 00:21:56,273
Trust me, I wish it was.

378
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:58,567
It'd make my marriage
a hell of a lot smoother.

379
00:21:58,608 --> 00:21:59,860
Your marriage is unsmooth?

380
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:03,655
The fact is, Macon hasn't done
anything illegal.

381
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:06,408
Now, he was cordial
when he needed you,

382
00:22:06,450 --> 00:22:07,784
but if you show up today

383
00:22:07,826 --> 00:22:11,246
with all your questions
and all your attitude,

384
00:22:11,246 --> 00:22:13,290
it is not gonna go well.

385
00:22:14,249 --> 00:22:15,542
Whose side are you on?

386
00:22:17,919 --> 00:22:21,006
-♪ (BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
-(SNIFFS, EXHALES SHARPLY)

387
00:22:24,926 --> 00:22:28,597
I'll take you,
but you let me do the talking.

388
00:22:29,639 --> 00:22:31,266
Understood?

389
00:22:31,266 --> 00:22:33,810
-Well, I don't know if I--
-Just nod.

390
00:22:36,438 --> 00:22:38,357
KERRY: Follow me.

391
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:40,025
♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

392
00:22:50,786 --> 00:22:51,536
Hey, Ben.

393
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:53,455
I'd like to see
your boss, please.

394
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:57,959
I'm afraid
he's not accepting visitors.

395
00:22:57,959 --> 00:23:00,295
Yeah, I get that. Absolutely.

396
00:23:00,337 --> 00:23:02,297
You know, sometimes
you just gotta accept things

397
00:23:02,297 --> 00:23:04,007
that take you
out of your comfort zone.

398
00:23:05,258 --> 00:23:06,676
Is he speaking for you?

399
00:23:06,718 --> 00:23:09,471
Right now,
he's pretty much just speaking.

400
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:12,391
This is part of
an official investigation, son.

401
00:23:13,433 --> 00:23:15,852
-Is that true?
-Evidently.

402
00:23:15,894 --> 00:23:17,979
Well, in that case,
can I see your warrant?

403
00:23:20,607 --> 00:23:23,527
Well, look at that. The cavalry.
Just in the nick of time.

404
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:28,490
(HORSE NEIGHS)

405
00:23:30,659 --> 00:23:33,328
The calvary's a lot faster
in the movies.

406
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:35,664
I told them
you aren't seeing any visitors.

407
00:23:36,373 --> 00:23:38,834
That's okay, Ben. Hey, Kerry.

408
00:23:40,001 --> 00:23:41,795
You know I'm a fan of your work.

409
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:44,673
But I confess, I'm confused
as to why you're still in town.

410
00:23:45,215 --> 00:23:46,466
Four aliens are dead.

411
00:23:46,508 --> 00:23:48,510
Their accomplice
blew himself up.

412
00:23:49,010 --> 00:23:50,345
And yet, you linger.

413
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:52,347
Well, that's what
your son told me.

414
00:23:52,347 --> 00:23:55,100
But, uh...
Well, here's what I think.

415
00:23:56,601 --> 00:23:58,270
I think you're hiding something
on this property

416
00:23:58,311 --> 00:23:59,521
you don't want me to see.

417
00:23:59,521 --> 00:24:01,231
I had you as a guest here
just the other day.

418
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:02,524
Because you wanted me to prove

419
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:04,526
that that fella
in custody was an alien.

420
00:24:04,568 --> 00:24:06,778
Which you did. Like I said,
I'm a fan of your work,

421
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:08,655
-but your work here's done.
-Oh, I just need a minute

422
00:24:08,697 --> 00:24:10,282
-of your time.
-I believe you've had it.

423
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:12,451
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

424
00:24:12,492 --> 00:24:14,536
Front gate, eleven o'clock.

425
00:24:14,536 --> 00:24:17,164
(RADIO BEEPING)

426
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:19,207
Oh, boy.
Am I about to be threatened?

427
00:24:19,207 --> 00:24:21,418
I got four dead bodies in my car

428
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:23,378
that set off
the hidden camera and alarm

429
00:24:23,378 --> 00:24:24,963
when I drag 'em
through those metal detectors

430
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:27,215
you got set up
at the stadium there.

431
00:24:27,215 --> 00:24:30,719
Now, I don't want to disparage
your small, little town,

432
00:24:30,719 --> 00:24:31,970
but I've been
all over the galaxy,

433
00:24:32,012 --> 00:24:33,722
and I don't think
I've ever seen technology

434
00:24:33,763 --> 00:24:35,098
quite that sophisticated.

435
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:38,518
I told you.

436
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:41,563
People who walked this land
before me,

437
00:24:41,605 --> 00:24:43,607
they got caught flat-footed
when the settlers come in

438
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:45,400
and colonized 'em.

439
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,360
I'm not about to make
that same mistake again.

440
00:24:47,402 --> 00:24:49,112
And how about that technology?

441
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:51,531
Very generous gift from the man
who funds this property.

442
00:24:51,573 --> 00:24:53,158
-Oh, your benefactor?
-WILL MACON: Correct.

443
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,534
Tell me the truth.
Is he even real,

444
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:56,244
or is this some
Keyser Söze situation?

445
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:57,579
Oh, I assure you,
he's very real.

446
00:24:57,579 --> 00:24:58,705
HAL:
Then what's his name again?

447
00:24:58,747 --> 00:24:59,873
I'm not at liberty to say.

448
00:24:59,915 --> 00:25:01,875
-Because of the NDA.
-WILL: That's right.

449
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:02,792
That's-- You know,

450
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:04,794
-do all cowboys have NDAs...
-That's it.

451
00:25:04,836 --> 00:25:06,588
-We're leaving.
-...or are you just
a special cowboy?

452
00:25:06,588 --> 00:25:07,923
No, I'm serious.

453
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:10,759
You got this whole Marlboro Man
thing happening here,

454
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:13,386
but yet you can't be straight
with me because of an NDA?

455
00:25:13,428 --> 00:25:14,888
Hell, even that other guy,

456
00:25:14,930 --> 00:25:16,598
he was selling cigarettes
to kids,

457
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:18,558
and he still didn't let
those lawyers stop him

458
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:20,644
from saying
whatever the hell he wanted.

459
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:26,066
I want to know
what other technology you got

460
00:25:26,107 --> 00:25:27,359
in this compound.

461
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:29,486
I think
it's important for you to know

462
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:31,279
there's a man with a rifle
in that guard tower

463
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:32,656
with instructions
to shoot anybody

464
00:25:32,697 --> 00:25:34,115
who trespasses on this property.

465
00:25:35,408 --> 00:25:36,993
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

466
00:25:38,036 --> 00:25:39,246
Well, you can't do that.

467
00:25:41,706 --> 00:25:45,335
-Can he do that?
-He can absolutely do that.

468
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:46,962
Well, that just seems
unneighborly.

469
00:25:47,462 --> 00:25:48,755
Sheriff.

470
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:50,465
HAL: I'm coming on.

471
00:25:50,465 --> 00:25:52,842
You're gonna have to deal
with me.

472
00:25:52,884 --> 00:25:54,886
Oh, for Christ's sake,
I got the ring.

473
00:25:54,928 --> 00:25:57,222
You try to shoot me,
and I'm just gonna put up--

474
00:25:57,264 --> 00:25:58,473
♪ (MUSIC STOPS ABRUPTLY) ♪

475
00:25:58,515 --> 00:26:01,893
-(CHAIR RATTLING)
-(JOHN BREATHING HEAVILY)

476
00:26:07,774 --> 00:26:09,985
I apologize for the violence.

477
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:13,822
-(BIRD CHIRPING)
-Yeah.

478
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:17,742
May I ask you a question
about the bird, John Stewart?

479
00:26:18,785 --> 00:26:19,619
Sure.

480
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:21,288
It's a wildly
impressive construct,

481
00:26:21,329 --> 00:26:22,831
but how does
Hal Jordan continue

482
00:26:22,831 --> 00:26:25,083
to project it
from such a great distance?

483
00:26:26,543 --> 00:26:28,837
He's not projecting it. I am.

484
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:30,672
You're not wearing a ring.

485
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:32,799
Did you tie me up
to ask me questions

486
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:34,009
about my fucking bird?

487
00:26:34,050 --> 00:26:36,970
No, I tied you up
to ask you about Manhunters.

488
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:44,060
I'm sorry.
Was I supposed to react?

489
00:26:44,102 --> 00:26:45,103
Yeah, you are.

490
00:26:45,145 --> 00:26:47,105
Because you think
I know what a Manhunter is?

491
00:26:47,147 --> 00:26:48,690
ANTAAN: Given your proximity
to Hal Jordan,

492
00:26:48,732 --> 00:26:50,400
it'd be very hard
to believe that you do not.

493
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:51,943
Proximity. You mean "closeness"?

494
00:26:51,985 --> 00:26:54,863
That's a better word, yes.
That's a much better word.

495
00:26:54,863 --> 00:26:58,700
JOHN: I see human
isn't your first language here.

496
00:26:58,742 --> 00:27:01,703
I'm not even close
to close with Hal Jordan.

497
00:27:01,745 --> 00:27:04,372
In fact, he sent me here
to get rid of me,

498
00:27:04,414 --> 00:27:05,665
so I'm sorry, gentlemen.

499
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:06,875
♪ (FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

500
00:27:06,916 --> 00:27:08,543
But you're about to torture
a man

501
00:27:08,543 --> 00:27:10,003
who doesn't know shit.

502
00:27:10,587 --> 00:27:16,343
(LAUGHS)

503
00:27:16,384 --> 00:27:18,511
Torture? No, John.

504
00:27:18,553 --> 00:27:20,055
We don't want
to torture you, John.

505
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:21,973
We want to recruit you.

506
00:27:23,975 --> 00:27:26,645
You don't tell someone
when you wanna recruit them.

507
00:27:27,520 --> 00:27:29,189
You have to be more subtle.

508
00:27:29,230 --> 00:27:30,899
ANTAAN: We don't have time
for subtlety, John.

509
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:33,109
One of the most dangerous beings
to ever exist

510
00:27:33,151 --> 00:27:35,403
knows it has been found,
which means right now

511
00:27:35,403 --> 00:27:36,988
it is preparing
its brutal response.

512
00:27:37,781 --> 00:27:39,032
And that's a Manhunter?

513
00:27:39,074 --> 00:27:40,909
You think the Green Lanterns
came first?

514
00:27:40,909 --> 00:27:43,078
-You really don't know?
-I really don't know.

515
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:44,746
Well, that makes things
much easier.

516
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:46,206
I don't have to change
your mind.

517
00:27:46,247 --> 00:27:47,415
I just need to stamp it.

518
00:27:47,457 --> 00:27:49,042
What the fuck
do you mean, stamp?

519
00:27:52,212 --> 00:27:54,589
Imprint? Um...

520
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:57,384
-Enlighten.
-I don't need enlightenment.

521
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:01,763
There was a time of chaos
in the galaxy.

522
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:04,599
-Then the Manhunters came.
-(MECHANISM CLICKING)

523
00:28:04,599 --> 00:28:05,934
ANTAAN: We don't know
where they came from,

524
00:28:05,975 --> 00:28:07,435
just that they were synthetic.

525
00:28:08,436 --> 00:28:09,688
And able to build new bodies,

526
00:28:09,729 --> 00:28:11,690
which meant they could take
the form of any species

527
00:28:11,731 --> 00:28:15,652
and embed, undetected,
within any society.

528
00:28:15,694 --> 00:28:17,445
This ability to build
allowed them

529
00:28:17,445 --> 00:28:18,780
to invent technologies

530
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:21,616
far beyond the limits
of the planets they inhabited.

531
00:28:21,658 --> 00:28:24,786
They were brutal.
They were deceptive.

532
00:28:24,786 --> 00:28:27,831
They carried out
what they called "justice."

533
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:30,500
Entire species were lost.

534
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:31,793
(DEVICE CLICKS, HUMS)

535
00:28:31,793 --> 00:28:33,420
ANTAAN: And then,
as mysteriously as they arrived,

536
00:28:33,461 --> 00:28:34,587
they were gone.

537
00:28:34,629 --> 00:28:36,631
At least
we thought they were gone.

538
00:28:36,631 --> 00:28:39,384
In reality, one of them remained
on our planet,

539
00:28:39,426 --> 00:28:40,510
passing as one of us

540
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:42,721
while he quietly engineered
a holocaust.

541
00:28:43,930 --> 00:28:45,974
Have you ever been deceived
by someone you love?

542
00:28:47,308 --> 00:28:48,268
Yeah.

543
00:28:48,309 --> 00:28:50,770
Then you'll understand
when you experience

544
00:28:51,646 --> 00:28:53,273
what he did to us.

545
00:28:55,984 --> 00:28:58,695
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

546
00:28:58,737 --> 00:29:00,155
(CHIRPING)

547
00:29:02,532 --> 00:29:05,243
Get off. (GRUNTS)

548
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:08,955
I'm sorry, but you need to see.

549
00:29:08,997 --> 00:29:11,916
-(DEVICE BUZZING)
-(GROANS)

550
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:13,960
-♪ (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING) ♪
-(SCREAMS)

551
00:29:14,002 --> 00:29:15,587
ANTAAN: This is what
it looks like

552
00:29:15,628 --> 00:29:18,089
when a Manhunter
destroys your people.

553
00:29:19,507 --> 00:29:21,551
John, do you see
what it feels like?

554
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:22,844
(JOHN SOBS)

555
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:25,096
-ANTAAN: See it!
-(GROANS)

556
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:27,474
ANTAAN: Do you see
what it did to them, John?

557
00:29:27,515 --> 00:29:30,685
-Do you see it?
-(SCREAMS)

558
00:29:30,727 --> 00:29:31,978
ANTAAN: See it!

559
00:29:32,854 --> 00:29:35,356
♪ (MUSIC RISES) ♪

560
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:37,233
-(DEVICE TURNS OFF)
-♪ (MUSIC FALLS) ♪

561
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:38,318
(PANTS)

562
00:29:41,029 --> 00:29:43,865
♪ (PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

563
00:29:47,535 --> 00:29:49,204
(GRUNTS)

564
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:55,710
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

565
00:29:55,710 --> 00:29:57,629
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

566
00:29:57,670 --> 00:29:59,255
The effects
of our collective loss

567
00:29:59,297 --> 00:30:01,299
will remain with you
for some time.

568
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:03,760
I'm sorry.

569
00:30:09,015 --> 00:30:10,725
The scale of our tragedy
drew the attention

570
00:30:10,767 --> 00:30:13,061
of a Green Lantern
sent by the Guardians.

571
00:30:14,103 --> 00:30:16,064
The Lantern

572
00:30:16,940 --> 00:30:18,650
took the monster
into his custody

573
00:30:18,691 --> 00:30:20,485
and guaranteed
he'd be executed.

574
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:25,198
-Why?
-ANTAAN: I do not know.

575
00:30:25,949 --> 00:30:27,367
It does not matter,

576
00:30:27,408 --> 00:30:29,369
but we believed, somewhere,
the Manhunter was still alive.

577
00:30:30,745 --> 00:30:35,124
So, we searched, John.
We searched for years.

578
00:30:35,166 --> 00:30:37,460
Until finally we discovered
where he was hiding.

579
00:30:39,379 --> 00:30:40,255
Rushville.

580
00:30:40,255 --> 00:30:42,215
ANTAAN:
Our detection is limited.

581
00:30:42,257 --> 00:30:44,300
There's radiation unique
to the Manhunter,

582
00:30:44,342 --> 00:30:46,219
though he could be disguised
as any human.

583
00:30:46,261 --> 00:30:49,180
To find out which,
we had to get close.

584
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:51,558
But our team was exposed
and killed.

585
00:30:54,102 --> 00:30:55,895
And who should arrive
an hour later?

586
00:30:56,437 --> 00:30:58,189
Jordan.

587
00:30:58,231 --> 00:31:00,441
You think he was trying
to protect the thing?

588
00:31:00,483 --> 00:31:01,651
ANTAAN: Perhaps.

589
00:31:01,693 --> 00:31:03,611
Our target knows
we've located him.

590
00:31:03,653 --> 00:31:06,197
And we cannot enter Rushville
without being detected.

591
00:31:06,239 --> 00:31:09,367
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

592
00:31:09,409 --> 00:31:10,451
So, you...

593
00:31:11,744 --> 00:31:13,955
you must identify the Manhunter.

594
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:18,459
How the fuck
am I supposed to do that?

595
00:31:18,459 --> 00:31:19,502
Your bird.

596
00:31:19,544 --> 00:31:21,880
This bird is proof
you can achieve the impossible.

597
00:31:22,839 --> 00:31:25,008
Now, we could fulfill
our mission

598
00:31:25,049 --> 00:31:27,760
by walking into the town square
and detonating ourselves,

599
00:31:27,802 --> 00:31:29,888
but that would destroy
Rushville.

600
00:31:31,139 --> 00:31:33,683
No reason for innocent lives
to be lost.

601
00:31:33,725 --> 00:31:37,145
Because it took a human form,
it could be killed as a human.

602
00:31:37,687 --> 00:31:39,856
You have 48 hours, John.

603
00:31:41,858 --> 00:31:43,234
Find the Manhunter.

604
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:48,323
Once you do...

605
00:31:50,283 --> 00:31:51,784
contact us.

606
00:31:51,826 --> 00:31:53,995
-If you fail to contact us--
-Yeah, I got it.

607
00:31:57,498 --> 00:31:59,000
♪ (MUSIC FADES) ♪

608
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:02,045
-(INHALES SHARPLY)
-(MONITOR BEEPING)

609
00:32:08,468 --> 00:32:09,510
KERRY: Hey, there.

610
00:32:12,847 --> 00:32:14,307
They shot me.

611
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:17,936
KERRY: You were trespassing.

612
00:32:17,977 --> 00:32:19,687
Might as well have walked
onto that ranch

613
00:32:19,729 --> 00:32:21,522
with a sign
that said, "Shoot me."

614
00:32:23,066 --> 00:32:26,027
-How are you feeling?
-Uh, all right.

615
00:32:26,027 --> 00:32:28,571
A little sore.
How long have I been out?

616
00:32:29,447 --> 00:32:32,241
Not too long.
They cleared you to go.

617
00:32:32,283 --> 00:32:34,619
Just wanted you
to sleep off the anesthesia.

618
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:39,165
(PANTS)

619
00:32:42,877 --> 00:32:44,128
So...

620
00:32:45,046 --> 00:32:47,340
what's with Sinestro?

621
00:32:48,758 --> 00:32:50,343
Why are you asking me that?

622
00:32:51,344 --> 00:32:53,972
KERRY: You kept saying his name
in your sleep.

623
00:32:55,890 --> 00:32:57,642
I'm not authorized
to talk about that.

624
00:32:59,185 --> 00:33:01,729
It's not exactly top secret.

625
00:33:03,564 --> 00:33:08,152
It says here, "He was a Lantern,
attempted a coup,

626
00:33:08,194 --> 00:33:11,364
killed one of the bosses."

627
00:33:11,406 --> 00:33:14,575
It also says you were the one
who took him down.

628
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:20,456
I don't talk about that.

629
00:33:20,498 --> 00:33:24,085
Except that you do,
in your sleep.

630
00:33:24,961 --> 00:33:26,254
-How...
-(HANDCUFF RATTLES)

631
00:33:29,090 --> 00:33:30,883
You gotta be kidding me.

632
00:33:30,925 --> 00:33:33,594
Like I said,
you were trespassing.

633
00:33:33,594 --> 00:33:34,929
HAL: In the name of Tom Osborne,

634
00:33:34,971 --> 00:33:36,764
or whoever it is
that you worship,

635
00:33:36,764 --> 00:33:38,474
please take these off.

636
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:43,062
Not until you listen to me.
Can you manage that?

637
00:33:43,604 --> 00:33:46,441
-Yes, ma'am.
-Good.

638
00:33:46,482 --> 00:33:48,735
Because every time
you don't listen,

639
00:33:48,776 --> 00:33:50,111
or you steal bodies,

640
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:52,697
or storm
my father-in-law's compound

641
00:33:52,739 --> 00:33:56,284
and don't let me do the talking,
what you're really doing

642
00:33:56,284 --> 00:33:58,661
is cutting my legs
straight out from under me.

643
00:33:59,787 --> 00:34:01,497
I'm the sheriff.

644
00:34:01,539 --> 00:34:04,959
If you don't follow my lead,
you're legitimizing this idea

645
00:34:04,959 --> 00:34:08,921
that Macon is the seat of power.
And trust me,

646
00:34:08,963 --> 00:34:11,716
you do not want to help
push that narrative.

647
00:34:13,468 --> 00:34:14,969
This is my town.

648
00:34:15,011 --> 00:34:17,597
I have worked my ass off
to earn people's respect,

649
00:34:17,638 --> 00:34:20,058
and I can't have you
undermining that.

650
00:34:23,144 --> 00:34:24,479
You're right.

651
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:29,275
I'm sorry. You're right.

652
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:35,865
So, you're gonna go back
to your motel

653
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:37,867
and let me do my job?

654
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:40,620
No more storming the compound?

655
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:44,499
I swear on Tom Osborne's life.

656
00:35:00,264 --> 00:35:01,599
(HANDCUFF UNLOCKS)

657
00:35:01,641 --> 00:35:04,352
And for the record,
I'm not on your side.

658
00:35:04,393 --> 00:35:07,522
I'm not on Macon's side.
I'm on my side,

659
00:35:07,563 --> 00:35:09,690
trying to hold
this town together.

660
00:35:14,445 --> 00:35:15,446
(SIGHS)

661
00:35:18,241 --> 00:35:20,326
Can I ask you a question?

662
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:22,537
If I knew
about the alien detectors,

663
00:35:22,578 --> 00:35:24,705
why did I fight you
on jurisdiction?

664
00:35:25,706 --> 00:35:27,208
Does make a guy wonder.

665
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:31,629
The others were dead.

666
00:35:31,671 --> 00:35:34,215
I assumed if Waylon
didn't set off the alarm,

667
00:35:34,215 --> 00:35:35,633
he wasn't an alien.

668
00:35:36,676 --> 00:35:37,718
I was wrong.

669
00:35:38,761 --> 00:35:39,804
It happens.

670
00:35:40,847 --> 00:35:43,432
KERRY: It shouldn't. Look.

671
00:35:43,474 --> 00:35:46,519
I apologize
for trying to obstruct you.

672
00:35:47,895 --> 00:35:49,939
I just didn't want Billy's dad

673
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:51,691
insurrecting the shit
out of everyone

674
00:35:51,732 --> 00:35:55,361
and getting them all paranoid
about invasion.

675
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:58,114
So much for that plan.

676
00:36:01,033 --> 00:36:02,743
Thanks for being straight
with me.

677
00:36:05,121 --> 00:36:07,832
Thanks for not dying
in my jurisdiction.

678
00:36:07,874 --> 00:36:08,875
(CHUCKLES DRYLY)

679
00:36:11,252 --> 00:36:12,920
KERRY: My turn for a question.

680
00:36:14,422 --> 00:36:17,133
Why am I still in town
if the threat's over?

681
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:19,468
It does make a girl wonder.

682
00:36:19,510 --> 00:36:22,763
Something is off here.
I can feel it.

683
00:36:26,809 --> 00:36:28,477
Why do you want me gone?

684
00:36:29,604 --> 00:36:32,231
Everything feels
like it's about to explode

685
00:36:32,273 --> 00:36:33,816
for no good reason.

686
00:36:34,859 --> 00:36:37,737
This place is losing its mind.

687
00:36:37,778 --> 00:36:41,282
You kicking up dust
and getting shot isn't helping.

688
00:36:43,784 --> 00:36:45,870
If I need you, I can call.

689
00:36:51,083 --> 00:36:52,627
You were at my bedside.

690
00:36:54,295 --> 00:36:56,339
It's a great book.

691
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:59,217
It's hard to find time
to read with a kid at home.

692
00:37:01,302 --> 00:37:05,556
-(TELEPHONE RINGING)
-♪ (BROODING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

693
00:37:17,276 --> 00:37:20,863
(SIGHS) So,
where are you from, anyway?

694
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:24,158
You decide
to actually make nice,

695
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,786
and that's the best you got?
"Where you from?"

696
00:37:26,827 --> 00:37:28,871
Well, you don't exactly
scream Rushville.

697
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:32,333
-(SCOFFS) You're a snob.
-Doesn't mean I'm wrong.

698
00:37:33,334 --> 00:37:37,004
I'm from Gotham.
Moved here on a whim.

699
00:37:37,046 --> 00:37:39,674
-That sounds like a story.
-Doesn't it?

700
00:37:41,425 --> 00:37:44,512
-That's all I'm gonna get?
-Pretty much.

701
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:47,014
Hmm. I'll take it for now.

702
00:37:47,014 --> 00:37:49,308
KERRY:
Because you're not leaving.

703
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:51,477
You didn't hear a word I said
in there, did you?

704
00:37:51,519 --> 00:37:54,480
Well, I heard a few of 'em.
Where are all the patients?

705
00:37:54,522 --> 00:37:57,441
It's a small town,
not exactly a big patient pool.

706
00:37:57,483 --> 00:37:59,443
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

707
00:37:59,485 --> 00:38:00,820
(SIGHS)

708
00:38:00,861 --> 00:38:01,737
Half the equipment looks

709
00:38:01,779 --> 00:38:03,531
like it was just taken out
of the crate.

710
00:38:03,531 --> 00:38:05,199
Yeah, well,
mostly everyone's smart enough

711
00:38:05,241 --> 00:38:06,826
not to get themselves shot.

712
00:38:08,035 --> 00:38:10,913
-(THUNDER RUMBLES)
-♪ (BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

713
00:38:18,379 --> 00:38:20,047
JOHN: Thank you.
Just over here is great.

714
00:38:26,053 --> 00:38:27,555
There you go. Thank you.

715
00:38:29,473 --> 00:38:31,309
-(BELL RINGING)
-(BIRD CHIRPS)

716
00:38:31,350 --> 00:38:34,061
♪ (SOFT COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS) ♪

717
00:38:34,061 --> 00:38:36,105
(FAINT CHATTER)

718
00:38:36,147 --> 00:38:37,356
(DOOR CLOSES)

719
00:38:40,568 --> 00:38:42,403
-(DOOR OPENS)
-(BELL RINGING)

720
00:38:42,403 --> 00:38:44,530
(GROANS) Hey.

721
00:38:44,572 --> 00:38:46,741
-Um, can I get a...
-(DOOR CLOSES)

722
00:38:46,741 --> 00:38:48,701
I... I'll get a decaf, please.
Thank you.

723
00:38:48,743 --> 00:38:50,953
-SERVER: Of course.
-(BIRD TWEETS)

724
00:38:50,995 --> 00:38:52,288
(COOKWARE CLANKING)

725
00:38:52,330 --> 00:38:54,915
-(JOHN SIGHS)
-(DOOR HINGES CREAKING)

726
00:39:03,090 --> 00:39:05,426
It's a small town,
bound to happen.

727
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:08,846
Yeah.

728
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:11,057
ZOE MACON: The booths
are more comfortable.

729
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:14,352
Uh, it's been a long day.

730
00:39:14,393 --> 00:39:17,396
I'm just trying to clear my head
for a second.

731
00:39:17,438 --> 00:39:19,273
Yeah, yeah. Fair enough.

732
00:39:19,273 --> 00:39:22,109
-(COFFEE POURING)
-(THUNDER RUMBLING)

733
00:39:25,821 --> 00:39:26,655
Thank you very much.

734
00:39:26,697 --> 00:39:28,074
-Here you go.
-JOHN: Thanks.

735
00:39:29,950 --> 00:39:32,953
(BIRD TWEETING)

736
00:39:53,724 --> 00:39:54,892
(SIGHS)

737
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:59,939
Um, for the record,

738
00:39:59,980 --> 00:40:02,650
I wouldn't have slept with you
if I knew you were married.

739
00:40:05,736 --> 00:40:07,863
Well, I'm glad you didn't know.

740
00:40:10,032 --> 00:40:11,992
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

741
00:40:11,992 --> 00:40:13,577
You into that kind of thing?

742
00:40:14,662 --> 00:40:16,455
ZOE: What kind of thing is that?

743
00:40:18,207 --> 00:40:19,708
I mean, uh...

744
00:40:20,835 --> 00:40:22,878
is your relationship
unconventional?

745
00:40:26,674 --> 00:40:28,050
You've met my husband, right?

746
00:40:28,092 --> 00:40:29,135
-JOHN: Mm-hmm.
-Mm-hmm.

747
00:40:29,176 --> 00:40:30,553
Yeah. What do you think?

748
00:40:30,594 --> 00:40:33,347
Uh, respectfully? I think
he's pretty fucking weird.

749
00:40:33,347 --> 00:40:35,850
(LAUGHS) Yeah, that he is.
Deeply so.

750
00:40:35,891 --> 00:40:37,852
Yeah. I think
he's pretty fucking weird,

751
00:40:37,852 --> 00:40:38,853
but you're not.

752
00:40:40,312 --> 00:40:42,064
(CUP CLINKS)

753
00:40:42,106 --> 00:40:46,318
-How can you be so sure?
-Uh, I see you. Um...

754
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:48,028
I don't think
you would do anything

755
00:40:48,028 --> 00:40:50,698
without thinking about it first.
You know?

756
00:40:50,698 --> 00:40:54,743
White men have the privilege
of being eccentric.

757
00:40:55,703 --> 00:40:57,705
White men with money?

758
00:40:57,746 --> 00:41:01,041
They can do
whatever the fuck they want.

759
00:41:01,083 --> 00:41:03,878
Play cowboy, build castles.

760
00:41:03,919 --> 00:41:07,506
-Do you like that?
-ZOE: Yeah. I like the security.

761
00:41:07,548 --> 00:41:08,883
I also like
that he could've bought

762
00:41:08,924 --> 00:41:11,093
some blonde bimbo from Texas
to be his arm candy,

763
00:41:11,135 --> 00:41:12,470
but he wanted me.

764
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:15,389
I'm sure a lot
of people want you.

765
00:41:15,431 --> 00:41:16,640
ZOE: None...

766
00:41:18,184 --> 00:41:19,852
that could give me what he has.

767
00:41:21,270 --> 00:41:22,313
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

768
00:41:22,354 --> 00:41:24,106
It's a lot to deal with,
I know, but...

769
00:41:25,065 --> 00:41:26,609
but it's worth it, I think.

770
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:30,154
And when I need a break,
I just take one.

771
00:41:30,196 --> 00:41:32,740
So, you'll put up with some
deeply weird White man

772
00:41:32,740 --> 00:41:34,909
with a savior complex
just to live the life?

773
00:41:34,950 --> 00:41:37,703
No, I'm with my husband
because I love him.

774
00:41:38,621 --> 00:41:40,206
And I know he loves me.

775
00:41:44,418 --> 00:41:46,003
Hey, how's your White man?

776
00:41:46,045 --> 00:41:47,171
(CHUCKLES)

777
00:41:47,922 --> 00:41:50,132
Uh, how is he?

778
00:41:51,592 --> 00:41:52,801
He wanted me out the way,

779
00:41:52,843 --> 00:41:55,679
so he, uh... he sent me
to fetch his things.

780
00:42:00,976 --> 00:42:04,104
Is that why you were trying
to clear your head over there?

781
00:42:08,484 --> 00:42:09,735
Uh...

782
00:42:11,570 --> 00:42:13,989
I'm just trying to figure out
if I can trust him.

783
00:42:14,031 --> 00:42:16,450
ZOE: If you have to ask
the question,

784
00:42:16,492 --> 00:42:19,078
then you already know
the answer.

785
00:42:22,665 --> 00:42:24,959
(CAR ENGINE RUMBLING)

786
00:42:33,092 --> 00:42:35,886
(BIRD CHIRPING)

787
00:42:45,020 --> 00:42:47,815
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

788
00:42:48,983 --> 00:42:50,025
JOHN: Nope.

789
00:42:51,819 --> 00:42:52,987
Don't.

790
00:42:57,783 --> 00:42:59,535
What happened to you?

791
00:42:59,577 --> 00:43:00,828
Your girlfriend's husband

792
00:43:00,869 --> 00:43:02,830
sicced one of you sniper-types
on me.

793
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:05,624
-Oh. Shoulder?
-HAL: Mm-hmm.

794
00:43:06,333 --> 00:43:08,168
Through and through?

795
00:43:08,168 --> 00:43:10,004
Yeah, it's a nice warning shot.

796
00:43:10,045 --> 00:43:11,839
Good to know
you're a fan of his work.

797
00:43:11,839 --> 00:43:14,258
-Yeah.
-(HAL GRUNTS)

798
00:43:15,843 --> 00:43:19,680
-(DISTANT TRAIN HORN BLARING)
-(ZIPPER OPENS)

799
00:43:24,518 --> 00:43:27,021
I told you
not to bring the suit.

800
00:43:27,062 --> 00:43:29,231
Yeah, well,
maybe I couldn't bring myself

801
00:43:29,273 --> 00:43:30,608
to just disrespect it.

802
00:43:30,649 --> 00:43:32,359
What else were you doing
while you were rummaging

803
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:33,694
through my stuff?

804
00:43:33,736 --> 00:43:36,697
Dance around in my bathrobes?
Sing into my hairbrush?

805
00:43:38,782 --> 00:43:39,867
(LANTERN WHIRRING)

806
00:43:39,908 --> 00:43:41,535
HAL: "In brightest day,
in blackest night,

807
00:43:41,535 --> 00:43:42,703
no evil shall escape my sight.

808
00:43:42,703 --> 00:43:43,996
Let those who worship
evil's might

809
00:43:44,038 --> 00:43:45,789
beware my power,
Green Lantern's light."

810
00:43:45,831 --> 00:43:47,875
-(WHIRRING STOPS)
-(SIGHS)

811
00:43:47,916 --> 00:43:49,960
There's something
on that compound.

812
00:43:50,544 --> 00:43:51,879
Benefactor's the key.

813
00:43:51,879 --> 00:43:54,381
We're not leaving here
until we find out who he is

814
00:43:54,423 --> 00:43:55,799
and what they're hiding.

815
00:43:55,841 --> 00:43:57,343
Yeah.

816
00:43:57,384 --> 00:44:00,596
-Whatever you say.
-(BIRD CHIRPING)

817
00:44:02,890 --> 00:44:04,933
HAL: Hey, you might want to, uh,

818
00:44:04,975 --> 00:44:07,728
check the fine print
on that insurance policy.

819
00:44:22,076 --> 00:44:24,203
What the hell's
all over the seats?

820
00:44:24,244 --> 00:44:27,873
I believe, uh, technically
they call that alien goo.

821
00:44:29,208 --> 00:44:30,209
(CAR DOOR CLOSES)

822
00:44:33,420 --> 00:44:34,630
(CAR DOOR SLAMS SHUT)

823
00:44:36,632 --> 00:44:37,591
(CHUCKLES)

824
00:44:37,633 --> 00:44:40,260
♪ (LOW TENSE MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

825
00:44:50,688 --> 00:44:52,439
What do you know
about Manhunters?

826
00:44:55,818 --> 00:44:57,277
Where'd you hear that word?

827
00:44:57,277 --> 00:45:00,155
Our buddy Waylon had friends.
They followed me onto the plane,

828
00:45:00,197 --> 00:45:02,157
snatched me outside
of your house.

829
00:45:02,199 --> 00:45:03,701
They're convinced
there's a Manhunter

830
00:45:03,742 --> 00:45:04,952
here in Rushville.

831
00:45:06,036 --> 00:45:07,162
(HAL GRUNTS)

832
00:45:11,041 --> 00:45:13,794
So, what did they want with you?

833
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:18,257
They want me to ID him.
And give him a call in 48 hours.

834
00:45:18,298 --> 00:45:21,301
Otherwise, they'll blow up
half of western Nebraska.

835
00:45:21,343 --> 00:45:22,553
Why you?

836
00:45:22,594 --> 00:45:25,639
Because they don't trust you.
In fact, he made it explicit

837
00:45:25,681 --> 00:45:27,516
that I shouldn't tell you
any of this.

838
00:45:27,558 --> 00:45:29,268
-What else?
-JOHN: Just that he thinks

839
00:45:29,309 --> 00:45:31,854
the Guardians
may have hid the Manhunter here.

840
00:45:31,895 --> 00:45:34,690
-They wouldn't do that.
-Well, shit. That's what I said.

841
00:45:34,732 --> 00:45:36,859
I knew there was something
about this place.

842
00:45:36,900 --> 00:45:39,153
And my gut is never wrong.

843
00:45:41,822 --> 00:45:43,323
(BIRD CHIRPING)

844
00:45:47,161 --> 00:45:48,871
Abin Sur must have brought
him here

845
00:45:48,912 --> 00:45:50,414
and the Manhunter killed him.

846
00:45:51,582 --> 00:45:54,001
Yeah, and then you got
your ring.

847
00:45:54,001 --> 00:45:56,420
What else can you tell me
about Manhunters?

848
00:45:56,462 --> 00:45:57,838
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

849
00:45:57,838 --> 00:45:59,173
It's above
your pay grade, Junior.

850
00:45:59,214 --> 00:46:02,301
JOHN: No, it's not.
I told you he was here.

851
00:46:02,342 --> 00:46:05,012
Oh, so now Mr. Chain of Command
wants me to break the rules?

852
00:46:05,053 --> 00:46:06,847
Hal, they don't know
what form he's taken.

853
00:46:06,889 --> 00:46:09,516
He could be anyone in town.

854
00:46:10,726 --> 00:46:12,895
♪ (MUSIC INTENSIFIES) ♪

855
00:46:12,936 --> 00:46:14,396
What else did they say to you?

856
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:19,067
You know, just that, um,

857
00:46:20,027 --> 00:46:22,571
to create a living thing,

858
00:46:22,613 --> 00:46:26,200
let alone keeping it alive
while not wearing the ring,

859
00:46:26,241 --> 00:46:27,618
is so advanced

860
00:46:27,659 --> 00:46:29,119
that it's practically
impossible.

861
00:46:29,161 --> 00:46:31,705
But I figured
that couldn't be true,

862
00:46:31,747 --> 00:46:33,707
'cause if it was,

863
00:46:33,749 --> 00:46:36,043
you would've at least given me
a hoorah.

864
00:46:38,045 --> 00:46:39,213
Hoorah.

865
00:46:45,594 --> 00:46:47,012
Forty-eight hours, huh?

866
00:46:48,639 --> 00:46:50,098
Yeah, 48.

867
00:46:50,140 --> 00:46:52,142
You tell the Guardians
any of this?

868
00:46:53,185 --> 00:46:55,521
(BIRD CHIRPING)

869
00:46:55,562 --> 00:46:57,064
JOHN: I report to you.

870
00:46:58,732 --> 00:47:00,359
-Hey.
-What?

871
00:47:01,902 --> 00:47:03,403
HAL:
What's with that bird, anyway?

872
00:47:03,403 --> 00:47:04,279
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

873
00:47:04,321 --> 00:47:06,114
-What are you talking about?
-The bird.

874
00:47:06,156 --> 00:47:08,075
I mean, you brought it to life
with your subconscious.

875
00:47:08,116 --> 00:47:10,327
It must mean
something pretty deep.

876
00:47:10,369 --> 00:47:11,411
It's just a bird.

877
00:47:12,538 --> 00:47:15,916
(CHIRPS)

878
00:47:15,916 --> 00:47:17,251
(CONSTRUCT WARBLES)

879
00:47:22,840 --> 00:47:27,553
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

880
00:47:27,594 --> 00:47:31,849
(DOOR OPENS, CLOSES)

881
00:47:34,768 --> 00:47:37,980
♪ (FAST-TEMPO
SYNTH MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

882
00:47:42,234 --> 00:47:43,277
(LANTERN CLANGS)

883
00:47:56,999 --> 00:48:00,043
♪ (DRAMATIC
SYNTH MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

884
00:48:09,469 --> 00:48:12,472
♪ (MUSIC BUILDS) ♪

885
00:48:31,408 --> 00:48:33,160
(CLANGING HUM)

886
00:48:34,953 --> 00:48:36,496
(CLANGING HUM)

887
00:48:39,958 --> 00:48:41,251
(DOOR HUMS)

888
00:48:41,293 --> 00:48:43,003
-Authorize Hal Jordan.
-♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

889
00:48:43,003 --> 00:48:44,463
AUTOMATED VOICE: Access granted.

890
00:48:46,590 --> 00:48:49,593
(CELL DOOR WHIRRING)

891
00:49:05,651 --> 00:49:06,652
Sinestro.

892
00:49:08,362 --> 00:49:09,363
Hal.

893
00:49:10,864 --> 00:49:12,532
Tell me what you know
about Manhunters.

894
00:49:12,574 --> 00:49:14,326
♪ ("HUMAN CONDITION"
BY PRETTY SICK PLAYING) ♪

895
00:49:14,368 --> 00:49:18,330
No hello?
No how have I been?

896
00:49:18,372 --> 00:49:20,499
HAL: Hello, Sinestro,
how have you been?

897
00:49:21,667 --> 00:49:24,127
Now, what the fuck do you know
about Manhunters?

898
00:49:25,212 --> 00:49:27,714
If one still existed,

899
00:49:27,756 --> 00:49:29,383
it'd be the second
greatest threat

900
00:49:29,424 --> 00:49:30,676
you're currently facing.

901
00:49:32,427 --> 00:49:34,429
So why don't you tell me
about John Stewart?

902
00:49:34,471 --> 00:49:37,599
♪ ("HUMAN CONDITION"
CONTINUES PLAYING) ♪

903
00:49:42,729 --> 00:49:45,273
♪ She takes my hand
And she pours me a glass ♪

904
00:49:45,315 --> 00:49:47,734
♪ Addiction's a disease
So, I get a pass ♪

905
00:49:47,734 --> 00:49:53,240
♪ I wanna feel something again ♪

906
00:49:53,240 --> 00:49:55,742
♪ She takes my hand
And she asks me to dance ♪

907
00:49:55,784 --> 00:49:58,120
♪ Nothing really matters
If you don't have romance ♪

908
00:49:58,161 --> 00:50:04,292
♪ I wanna feel something again ♪

909
00:50:14,386 --> 00:50:16,513
♪ He takes me out and says
"Let's do business" ♪

910
00:50:16,555 --> 00:50:19,266
♪ He's a bad guy
But I believe in forgiveness ♪

911
00:50:19,266 --> 00:50:23,729
♪ I wanna do something
That matters ♪

912
00:50:25,063 --> 00:50:26,857
♪ Takes a meeting
'Cause he likes my vision ♪

913
00:50:26,898 --> 00:50:29,609
♪ I'm not opportunistic
No, I'm just ambitious ♪

914
00:50:29,651 --> 00:50:35,782
♪ I wanna be someone
That matters ♪

915
00:50:55,802 --> 00:50:58,346
♪ The freedom you're being sold
Is just submission ♪

916
00:50:58,388 --> 00:51:01,224
♪ They wanna keep you content
And under supervision ♪

917
00:51:01,266 --> 00:51:03,643
♪ They got you convinced
That ignorance is bliss in ♪

918
00:51:03,685 --> 00:51:07,105
♪ Some ever changing mind
Erasing human condition ♪

919
00:51:07,147 --> 00:51:12,652
♪ I don't have time
To worry about ♪

920
00:51:12,652 --> 00:51:17,866
♪ If I am stuck
And if there's any way out ♪

921
00:51:17,908 --> 00:51:23,080
♪ I don't have time ♪

922
00:51:23,121 --> 00:51:28,335
♪ I don't have time ♪

923
00:51:29,711 --> 00:51:31,421
♪ (SONG CONCLUDES) ♪

